{
  "dom_id": "step-q252041",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Let the random variable $Y$ be defined as\n\n$$\nY={Z}_{1}^{2}+{Z}_{2}^{2}+⋯+{Z}_{50}^{2}\n$$\n\nwhere ${Z}_{i}∼N(0,1)$ for $1\\le i\\le 50.$ Find the value $y$ such that $P(Y\\le y)=0.85.$\n\n*Hint: The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X∼{χ}^{2}(k).$*\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.010$ | $0.050$ | $0.100$ | $0.150$ | $0.200$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $48$ | $\\,73.683\\,$ | $\\,65.171\\,$ | $\\,60.907\\,$ | $\\,58.135\\,$ | $\\,55.993\\,$ |\n| $49$ | $\\,74.919\\,$ | $\\,66.339\\,$ | $\\,62.038\\,$ | $\\,59.241\\,$ | $\\,57.079\\,$ |\n| $50$ | $\\,76.154\\,$ | $\\,67.505\\,$ | $\\,63.167\\,$ | $\\,60.346\\,$ | $\\,58.164\\,$ |\n\nThe value of $y$ that satisfies $P(Y\\le y)=0.85$ is $y=$\n{{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "If ${Z}_{i}∼N(0,1)$ for $1\\le i\\le k$ are independent normal random variables, then the sum\n\n$$\n{Z}_{1}^{2}+{Z}_{2}^{2}+⋯+{Z}_{k}^{2}\n$$\n\nfollows a ${χ}^{2}(k)$ distribution with $k$ degrees of freedom.\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\nY={Z}_{1}^{2}+{Z}_{2}^{2}+⋯+{Z}_{50}^{2}∼{χ}^{2}(50).\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the given probability in the form $P(Y\\ge y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\le y) & =1-P(Y\\ge y) \\\\ 0.85 & =1-P(Y\\ge y) \\\\ P(Y\\ge y) & =0.15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we wish to find the value $y$ such that $P(Y\\ge y)=0.15$ This can be found from the given table:\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.010$ | $0.050$ | $0.100$ | $0.150$ | $0.200$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $48$ | $\\,73.683\\,$ | $\\,65.171\\,$ | $\\,60.907\\,$ | $\\,58.135\\,$ | $\\,55.993\\,$ |\n| $49$ | $\\,74.919\\,$ | $\\,66.339\\,$ | $\\,62.038\\,$ | $\\,59.241\\,$ | $\\,57.079\\,$ |\n| $50$ | $\\,76.154\\,$ | $\\,67.505\\,$ | $\\,63.167\\,$ | $\\,60.346\\,$ | $\\,58.164\\,$ |\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(Y\\ge 60.346)=0.15\n$$\n\nwhich means\n\n$$\nP(Y\\le 60.346)=0.85.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=60.346.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
